{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/events/fruit.js';s=open(p).read();start=s.index('for(const p of l.fruit){if(\"'!p.active||p.caught||p.spent||this.t>p.landing)continue;'\"');end=s.index('if(this.t>=d.next)',start);s=s[:start]+s[end:];s=s.replace(\\\"const incoming=p.body.linvel();p.body.setLinvel({x:incoming.x*.08,y:Math.max(incoming.y,-.8),z:incoming.z*.08},true);\\\",'');start=s.index(' botInput(l,t,skill=');end=s.index('\\\\n botActions',start);s=s[:start]+s[end:];open(p,'w').write(s)\np='notes/issues.md';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace('- 20 [balance] The integrated fruit flights carried too much sideways speed into the hat. Gave their arc a soft horizontal finish and a cushioned first catch; their weight and motion inside the hat remain dynamic Rapier contacts.', '- Diagnostic experiment (not counted): tried soft flight finishes and catch cushioning while isolating Fruit Hat instability. Restored ballistic flights and real catch impulses after fixing retired-body contacts.')\ns=s.replace('- Diagnostic hardening (not counted): disabled props leave cached contact manifolds in Rapier. Prop retirement now removes the body and its references; reusable ragdoll colliders are explicitly disabled. Testing did not establish cached manifolds as the cause of a gameplay fault.', '- 20 [critical physics] Disabled fruit retained contacts and the hat behaved as though banked loads were still attached. Removing retired prop bodies and clearing references fixed the three-seed balance tests; never banking still spills. Reusable ragdoll colliders are also explicitly disabled.')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/art/island.js';s=open(p).read().replace('ConeGeometry(19.5,6.8,14)','ConeGeometry(19.5,11,14)').replace('root,0,-4.9,0','root,0,-6.3,0').replace('root,0,-8.5,0,2.3','root,0,-12.8,0,2.3');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/game/island.js';s=open(p).read().replace('sea.position.y=-9.2','sea.positi