{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_129","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cp /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0 vendor/APACHE-2.0.txt\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='tools/build.mjs';s=open(p).read();needle=\\\"const out=['<\"'!doctype html>\";s=s.replace(needle,\"const notices=JSON.stringify({ThreeJS:readFileSync('\"'node_modules/three/LICENSE','utf8'),Rapier:readFileSync('vendor/APACHE-2.0.txt','utf8'),Fredoka:readFileSync('node_modules/@fontsource/fredoka/LICENSE','utf8')}).replace(/<\\\\\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\/script');\\\\nconst out=['<\"'!doctype html>\")\ns=s.replace(\"</small></div><script>'\"',js\\\", \\\"</small></div><script type=\\\\\\\"application/json\\\\\\\" id=\\\\\\\"third-party-notices\\\\\\\">',notices,'</script><script>',js\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Wee Knit\n\nOpen the HTML in the parent folder directly. Everything is embedded; it works offline. A controller or keyboard is required. Touch devices show Settings and an automatic demonstration.\n\nA five-day wooden-toy retreat with fourteen activities, daily Check-Ins, imaginary Wobble Ages, a physical marble jar, unlockable hats, a walking island, an ending and continuing Maintenance days. Every class shares a Rapier balance core. Falls become floor exercises.\n\n- Controller: left stick leans or walks; L2/R2 are feet; Cross hops/banks or confirms; Square flails; R1 breathes; Triangle opens today's plan; Options pauses. The right stick orbits on the island.\n- Keyboard: WASD/arrows move the asking ring, which stays where you leave it; C recentres. Q/E are feet, Space hops/banks, F flails, Shift breathes, Enter confirms, T opens the plan, Esc pauses. Walking uses direct keys.\n- Mouse: pointer position leans; left/right buttons are feet; both hop/bank; middle flails. On the island, click a landmark to walk there; right drag orbits and the wheel zooms.\n\nProgramme progress never requires a medal. Going to bed ends the day. Free Play offers unlocked classes and medal-based difficulty tiers. Group Class supports four local seats and three-class playlists. AI Hub sessions use the released 1.4.0 client and a synchronized three-class ghost round.\n\nPause → Dev Mode offers event/day/step jumps, live tuning, resets, forced falls/props/gusts, time scale, single steps, a bot, stats/input, physics lines, a free camera, rewards, palettes and JSON tuning export. Settings include sound, PlayStation/Xbox glyphs, auto-breathing, rhythm offset, ink and difficulty.\n\n## Development\n\n\"'`npm install` installs the pinned dependencies. `npm run build` emits `game.html` here and the named deliverable in the parent folder, embedding the parent `exit-interview.json` into About/Credits. Data for events, days, charts, poses, dialogue, names, unlocks and live tuning lives in `src/data/`.\n\n`node tools/test.mjs full` runs the whole-programme playthrough, every event/tier, balance simulations, inputs, offline audio, save/UI checks, WebGPU/WebKit, the viewport matrix, art snapshots and the real AI Hub harness. It prints failures and one result count. Specific groups can be selected. Browsers run serially; the hub server binds an OS-selected loopback port and closes itself.\n\n`?test=1&render=0&manual=1` exposes deterministic test hooks without a renderer. Without these parameters the game runs normally. Test artifacts and the issue log are in `notes/`; inspected art and viewport captures are in `shots/`.\n\nThird-party notices are embedded in the single HTML: Three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Fredoka (SIL OFL). Models, text, music, effects and gibberish voices are generated in code. No images or audio recordings are downloaded.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs unit flow input ui'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_129","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cp /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0 vendor/APACHE-2.0.txt\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='tools/build.mjs';s=open(p).read();needle=\\\"const out=['<\"'!doctype html>\";s=s.replace(needle,\"const notices=JSON.stringify({ThreeJS:readFileSync('\"'node_modules/three/LICENSE','utf8'),Rapier:readFileSync('vendor/APACHE-2.0.txt','utf8'),Fredoka:readFileSync('node_modules/@fontsource/fredoka/LICENSE','utf8')}).replace(/<\\\\\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\/script');\\\\nconst out=['<\"'!doctype html>\")\ns=s.replace(\"</small></div><script>'\"',js\\\", \\\"</small></div><script type=\\\\\\\"application/json\\\\\\\" id=\\\\\\\"third-party-notices\\\\\\\">',notices,'</script><script>',js\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Wee Knit\n\nOpen the HTML in the parent folder directly. Everything is embedded; it works offline. A controller or keyboard is required. Touch devices show Settings and an automatic demonstration.\n\nA five-day wooden-toy retreat with fourteen activities, daily Check-Ins, imaginary Wobble Ages, a physical marble jar, unlockable hats, a walking island, an ending and continuing Maintenance days. Every class shares a Rapier balance core. Falls become floor exercises.\n\n- Controller: left stick leans or walks; L2/R2 are feet; Cross hops/banks or confirms; Square flails; R1 breathes; Triangle opens today's plan; Options pauses. The right stick orbits on the island.\n- Keyboard: WASD/arrows move the asking ring, which stays where you leave it; C recentres. Q/E are feet, Space hops/banks, F flails, Shift breathes, Enter confirms, T opens the plan, Esc pauses. Walking uses direct keys.\n- Mouse: pointer position leans; left/right buttons are feet; both hop/bank; middle flails. On the island, click a landmark to walk there; right drag orbits and the wheel zooms.\n\nProgramme progress never requires a medal. Going to bed ends the day. Free Play offers unlocked classes and medal-based difficulty tiers. Group Class supports four local seats and three-class playlists. AI Hub sessions use the released 1.4.0 client and a synchronized three-class ghost round.\n\nPause → Dev Mode offers event/day/step jumps, live tuning, resets, forced falls/props/gusts, time scale, single steps, a bot, stats/input, physics lines, a free camera, rewards, palettes and JSON tuning export. Settings include sound, PlayStation/Xbox glyphs, auto-breathing, rhythm offset, ink and difficulty.\n\n## Development\n\n\"'`npm install` installs the pinned dependencies. `npm run build` emits `game.html` here and the named deliverable in the parent folder, embedding the parent `exit-interview.json` into About/Credits. Data for events, days, charts, poses, dialogue, names, unlocks and live tuning lives in `src/data/`.\n\n`node tools/test.mjs full` runs the whole-programme playthrough, every event/tier, balance simulations, inputs, offline audio, save/UI checks, WebGPU/WebKit, the viewport matrix, art snapshots and the real AI Hub harness. It prints failures and one result count. Specific groups can be selected. Browsers run serially; the hub server binds an OS-selected loopback port and closes itself.\n\n`?test=1&render=0&manual=1` exposes deterministic test hooks without a renderer. Without these parameters the game runs normally. Test artifacts and the issue log are in `notes/`; inspected art and viewport captures are in `shots/`.\n\nThird-party notices are embedded in the single HTML: Three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Fredoka (SIL OFL). Models, text, music, effects and gibberish voices are generated in code. No images or audio recordings are downloaded.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs unit flow input ui'","aggregated_output":"Wee-Knit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-232145.html · 3.18 MB\nFAIL input paths: locator.click: Timeout 30000ms exceeded.\nCall log:\n\u001b[2m  - waiting for locator('button').filter({ hasText: 'Live tuning' }).first()\u001b[22m\n\n204 passed, 1 failed\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_130","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > src/render/ink.js <<'EOF'\nimport * as T from 'three/webgpu';\nimport {uniform,vec4,positionLocal,normalLocal,cameraProjectionMatrix,modelViewMatrix,normalize,time,sin} from 'three/tsl';\n// Draw the ink hull and the cel surface together. This keeps newly built sets in\n// the same native render traversal as the scenery, lights and moving characters.\nexport function makeInk(renderer,scene,camera){\n const u={hull:uniform(.0028),width:uniform(1.2),boil:uniform(.35),grain:uniform(.015),near:uniform(camera.near),far:uniform(camera.far),ink:uniform(new T.Color(0x26232e))},stats={sceneFrames:0},outlines=new WeakMap();\n function outlineFor(original){let m=outlines.get(original);if(m)return m;m=new T.NodeMaterial();m.name='Retreat ink hull';m.side=T.BackSide;const mvp=cameraProjectionMatrix.mul(modelViewMatrix),p=mvp.mul(vec4(positionLocal,1)),p2=mvp.mul(vec4(positionLocal.add(normalLocal.negate()),1)),n=normalize(p.sub(p2)),boil=sin(time.mul(8)).mul(u.boil).mul(.08).add(1);m.vertexNode=p.add(n.mul(u.hull).mul(u.width.div(1.2)).mul(boil).mul(p.w));m.colorNode=vec4(u.ink,1);outlines.set(original,m);return m;}\n const render=()=>{const previous=renderer.getRenderObjectFunction();renderer.setRenderObjectFunction((object,sc,cam,geometry,material,group,lights,clip)=>{if(material.isMeshToonNodeMaterial&&material.wireframe===false&&u.hull.value>0)renderer.renderObject(object,sc,cam,geometry,outlineFor(material),group,lights,clip);renderer.renderObject(object,sc,cam,geometry,material,group,lights,clip);});renderer.render(scene,camera);renderer.setRenderObjectFunction(previous);stats.sceneFrames++;};\n return {u,stats,scene,render};\n}\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='src/render/renderer.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"this.ink?.post.dispose();this.ink?.pass.dispose();\\\",'').replace(\\\"this.ink.pass.updateBefore({renderer:this.renderer});this.ink.post.render();\\\", \\\"this.ink.render();\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"this.renderer.domElement.id='world';await this.renderer.init();\\\", \\\"this.renderer.domElement.id='world';this.paper=document.createElement('div');this.paper.id='paper-grain';this.paper.innerHTML='<svg width=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\" aria-hidden=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\"><filter id=\\\\\\\"paper-noise\\\\\\\"><feTurbulence type=\\\\\\\"fractalNoise\\\\\\\" baseFrequency=\\\\\\\".68\\\\\\\" numOctaves=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" stitchTiles=\\\\\\\"stitch\\\\\\\"/></filter><rect width=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\" filter=\\\\\\\"url(#paper-noise)\\\\\\\" opacity=\\\\\\\".5\\\\\\\"/></svg>';document.body.append(this.paper);await this.renderer.init();\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"u.grain.value=tuning.grain;\\\", \\\"u.grain.value=tuning.grain;if(this.paper)this.paper.style.opacity=String(tuning.grain*1.7);\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tools/shots.mjs';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"g.view.ink.pass.updateBefore({renderer:g.view.renderer});await g.view.ink.post.renderAsync();\\\", \\\"g.view.render();\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tools/test.mjs';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"v.ink.pass.scene===v.scene\\\", \\\"v.ink.scene===v.scene\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat >> src/ui/ui.css <<'EOF'\n#paper-grain{position:fixed;inset:0;pointer-events:none;z-index:1;opacity:.025;mix-blend-mode:multiply}#ui{z-index:2}\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs render visual\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
